# Everything here is optional. Rename this file to `linkedin.md` to switch it
# on; `cvme linkedin` picks it up from beside the resume with no configuration.
#
# This is a patch over `resume.md`, not a second resume. Write only the parts
# that should read differently on a profile that has no page to fit. Anything
# left out comes from the resume, which stays the single source of truth.
#
# The headline LinkedIn shows under your name, up to 220 characters. Without
# one, cvme uses your current role, the same as LinkedIn does.
headline: Your Role | What you build | The three tools you want to be found for
---

## Summary

This replaces the resume's summary in the About section, where you have 2,600
characters instead of four lines. Say what you work on, who it is for, and what
you are looking for next.

Blank lines survive, so this can be several paragraphs.

## Experience

### Your Role @ Your Employer | Mon YYYY – Present

The entry header must match the resume's -- role, organisation and start date
-- or this is added as a second job rather than replacing the first one. The
end date is not matched on, so "Present" here and a real date there is fine.

- Every bullet the page could not fit
- Up to 2,000 characters per role, against a resume's five lines
- Bullets that would have been cut for length rather than for being untrue
